> HE
MON68K commands (numbers are hex; #dec %bin 'c' .reg; + and - allowed)
 MD [addr [len]]          memory dump (Enter continues)
 MM[.B/.W/.L] addr [v..]  modify memory; no values: interactive
                          (Enter next, - back, . quit)
 MF[.B/.W/.L] start end v fill memory
 MC start end dest        copy memory (overlap safe)
 MS[.B/.W/.L] start end v [v..]  search;  MS start end "text"
 CM start end dest        compare memory
 LO [offset]              load S-records (S1/S2/S3, S5/S6, S7/S8/S9)
 DU start end [entry]     dump memory as S-records
 GO [addr]                run (from addr, or continue)
 GT addr                  run until addr
 CALL addr                call a subroutine; RTS returns to the monitor
 T [n]                    trace n instructions (Enter repeats)
 SO                       step over BSR/JSR/TRAP
 R  /  R reg value        show / set registers (D0-D7 A0-A7 SP PC SR USP SSP)
 RI                       reset program registers to defaults
 BR [addr [count]]        set / list breakpoints (8)
 BC [n | addr]            clear one / all breakpoints
 DI [addr [n]]            disassemble (Enter continues)
 VE [D]                   list changed exception vectors (D: restore all)
 IN                       memory map and status
 BA [top]                 EhBASIC, cold start (RAM $01000 to top-1)
 BW [start]               EhBASIC, warm start (keeps the program)
Ctrl-C or BREAK stops a running program; NMI too. Programs call the monitor
with TRAP #15 (D0.W = function), see MONITOR.md.
